      "displayName": "A. Soroka",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A24c578cc-15e9-4649-9f68-5eace85735e0",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>One helpful resource Fedora could offer is simply a list of currently non-OSGi dependencies. It might even be possible to pull this out of Maven build information... For those of us looking to platforms like Apache Karaf, this would enable us to use Karaf's feature-provisioning abilities to automatically wrap and deploy non-OSGi libraries, right off of that list. People using other OSGi systems could use Pax Wrap for a similar action.</p>",
     "created": "20/Feb/11 5:46 PM",
